  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Jesus Children** (1 review, 1 other source): Reviewer singles out the Jesus Children into Who Knows and back into Jesus Children sequence as the highlight; Jesus Children flows into Who Knows, then returns to Jesus Children [2][4]\n- **Doin Somethin'** (1 other source): Doin' Something runs into Chameleon, then returns to Doin' Something [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Doin Somethin'**: rare: 7 archived performances [5]\n- **Doin Somethin'**: rare: 7 archived performances [5]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: One in Seven [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **SouliveTheAvalonBostonMa10-20-2000** (recommended): soundboard; 14 songs; 91 min [1]\n- **Soulive2000-10-20.Boston**: audience recording; 10 songs; 94 min [3]\n- **soulive2000-10-20.shnf**: source not stated; 14 songs; 94 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer prefers the original trio lineup over later versions of the band that added horn sections [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **SouliveTheAvalonBostonMa10-20-2000**: taped by ?; transferred by Nate Bourgault; source: SBD>DAT>1st Gen analog [1]\n- **Soulive2000-10-20.Boston**: taped by Peter Costello and Eric McRoberts; transferred by Paul deLima; source: Schoeps CMC6/MK21 (on stage, configured at 95 degrees) + Oktava MC-012 (on stage, split 20 feet & facing the audience) > Mackie 1202-VLZ > (50/50 mix of the… [3]. Also: Chain: Mackie mixer, Apogee AD-1000, Tascam DAT, Fostex D-5, Roland R-44, Cool Edit Pro editing, then FLAC; Edits included fades and clipping restoration; Schoeps mics were configured at 95 degrees on a stand [3]\n- **soulive2000-10-20.shnf**: taped by Pete Costello; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: (On Stage) Schoeps cmc621(95 degrees, 4' high, 50%)+ (On Stage) Oktava MC 012(omnis, split ~20-25', 50%)->Mackie 1202vlz->Apogee AD-1000(+4dB, @44.1kHz) [2]",
